// A TAIL that lets holders melt their own tokens, and delegates issuance to another TAIL.
//
// Any negative supply change is allowed without conditions. Other supply changes are passed to the
// curried issuance TAIL, with the rest of the solution. For example, wrapping `genesis_by_coin_id`
// gives a fixed supply that can only go down, as tokens are burned.
//
// Melting still requires spending the DOG coin, so it needs the owner's inner puzzle, and a negative
// supply change requires a lineage proof (without one, the supply change is the amount of the
// execution coin, which can't be negative). Since the owner's inner puzzle usually signs the
// execution coin's id with `AGG_SIG_ME`, and the id includes the amount after melting, only the owner
// can melt their tokens.
//
// Inner puzzles that don't sign the execution coin's id can be melted by anyone, as far as their
// other conditions allow, while they're in the mempool. For example, if a settlement payments coin
// pays out less than its amount in an offer, the rest could be burned by anyone. That loses the
// tokens, but nobody gains anything from it.

type Tail = fn(
    supply_change: Int,
    new_amount: Int,
    inner_puzzle_hash: Bytes32,
    asset_id: Bytes32,
    ...solution: Any,
) -> List<Condition>;

fn main(
    issuance_tail: Tail,
    supply_change: Int,
    new_amount: Int,
    inner_puzzle_hash: Bytes32,
    asset_id: Bytes32,
    ...solution: Any,
) -> List<Condition> {
    if supply_change < 0 {
        return nil;
    }
    issuance_tail(supply_change, new_amount, inner_puzzle_hash, asset_id, ...solution)
}
